# Arch Linux ARM package signing trust root.
#
# Arch Linux ARM signs its packages with a key that archlinux-keyring does not
# carry, so a build host that only trusts archlinux-keyring rejects every ARM
# package. Pinning the keyring package, its checksum and its trusted key set
# here lets SigLevel = Required stay on with no signature weakening.
#
# bootstrap/any/usr/local/bin/install-port-keyring reads every .pin in this
# directory and uses the one whose arch list carries the Architecture of the
# build. Adding a port means adding a file here, not editing that script.
#
# Fields:
#   keyring   the pacman keyring name, so --populate can be told what to add
#   arch      the pacman Architecture values this pin serves, space separated
#   mirror    the directory the package is fetched from
#   package   the pinned package, name carrying its version
#   sha256    over that package
#   trusted   one line per fingerprint in the keyring's own -trusted file,
#             with the primary key's expiry as YYYY-MM-DD or never
#
# ⛔ The trusted lines are a set, and the whole set is asserted. A fingerprint
# added, removed or re-dated is the trust root moving, and it stops the build
# rather than passing quietly.
#
# To re-derive, from any host:
#   curl -sSL -o k.pkg.tar.xz http://mirror.archlinuxarm.org/aarch64/core/<package>
#   sha256sum k.pkg.tar.xz
#   bsdtar -xOf k.pkg.tar.xz usr/share/pacman/keyrings/archlinuxarm-trusted
#   bsdtar -xOf k.pkg.tar.xz usr/share/pacman/keyrings/archlinuxarm.gpg | \
#     gpg --with-colons --show-keys
#
# Adopted 2026-08-26. Trusted set and expiry re-measured 2026-08-28 against
# http://mirror.archlinuxarm.org/aarch64/core/.

keyring = archlinuxarm
arch    = aarch64 armv7h
mirror  = http://mirror.archlinuxarm.org/aarch64/core
package = archlinuxarm-keyring-20240419-2-any.pkg.tar.xz
sha256  = 3cb36869edfe413672a6e932cc55d7f8386e1a9d3b38663cfb3bc6fe0d146e21
trusted = 68B3537F39A313B3E574D06777193F152BDBE6A6 never
